  "result": "A new chemically-defined medium for RAC-certified and other strains of Bacillus subtilis | Applied Microbiology and Biotechnology | Springer Nature Link (https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF00264002)\nciteturn42view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF00264002\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 198\nL0: Account\nL1: \nL2: 【0†Menu】\nL3: \nL4: 【1†Find a journal】 【2†Publish with us†www.springernature.com】 【3†Track your research†link.springernature.com】\nL5: \nL6: 【4†Search】\nL7: \nL8: 【5†Saved research】\nL9: \nL10: 【6†Cart†order.springer.com】\nL11: # A new chemically-defined medium for RAC-certified and other strains of Bacillus subtilis\nL12: \nL13:   * Applied Genetics and Regulation\nL14:   * Published: February 1989\nL15: \nL16:   * Volume 30, pages 144–147 (1989)\nL17:   * 【7†Cite this article】\nL18: \nL19: [Input] Save article\nL20: \nL21: 【5†View saved research】\nL22: \nL23: 【8†Applied Microbiology and Biotechnology】 【9†Aims and scope】 【10†Submit manuscript†submission.springernature.com】\nL24: \nL25:   * 【11†AiQi Fang】^{【12†1】}^{ 【13†nAff2】} &\nL26:   * 【14†Arnold L. Demain】^{【12†1】}\nL27: \nL28:   * 164 Accesses\nL29: \nL30:   * 7 Citations\nL31:   * 【15†Explore all metrics】\nL32: ## Summary\nL33: Conventional chemically-defined media were found to be inadequate for extensive batch culture growth of an asporogenous mutant of Bacillus subtilis certified as an HV-1 host for recombinant DNA. We developed a chemically-defined medium for rapid and extensive growth of one such strain, BGSC-1S53. The medium contains no components requiring separate sterilization.\nL34: It is also useful for the prototrophic 168 strain (from which 1S53 was derived), a triple auxotroph of 168, and a highly debilitated (HV-2) 168 strain (BGSC 1S76) upon addition of the specific growth factors required by these strains. Excellent growth was also obtained with W-23, a Bacillus subtilis strain unrelated to the 168 series.\nL35: This is a preview of subscription content, to check access.\nL36: ## Access this article\nL37: \nL38: Log in via an institution\nL39: \nL40: ## Subscribe and save\nL41: \nL42: Springer+\nL43: \nL44: from $39.99 /Month\nL45: \nL46:   * Starting from 10 chapters or articles per month\nL47:   * Access and download chapters and articles from more than 300k books and 2,500 journals\nL48:   * Cancel anytime\nL49: 【16†View plans】\nL50: ## Buy Now\nL51: \nL52: [Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input]\nL53: \nL54: Buy article PDF USD 39.95\nL55: \nL56: Price excludes VAT (USA)\nL57: Tax calculation will be finalised during checkout.\nL58: \nL59: Instant access to the full article PDF.\nL60: \nL61: 【17†Institutional subscriptions†www.springernature.com】\nL62: \nL63: ### Similar content being viewed by others\nL64: \nL65: 【18†Image†media.springernature.com】\nL66: ### 【19†Bacillus subtilis: a universal cell factory for industry, agriculture, biomaterials and medicine】\nL67: \nL68: Article Open access 03 September 2020\nL69: \nL70: 【20†Image†media.springernature.com】\nL71: \nL72: ### 【21†Whole-genome sequencing and comparative genomic analysis of a novel Bacillus subtilis strain YE16 isolated from yak dung】\nL73: \nL74: Article Open access 29 June 2026\nL75: \nL76: 【22†Image†media.springernature.com】\nL77: ### 【23†Engineering Bacillus subtilis for high-value bioproduction: recent advances and applications】\nL78: \nL79: Article Open access 12 August 2025\nL80: ## References\nL81: \nL82:   * Anagnostopoulos C, Spezizen J (1961) Requirements for transformation in Bacillus subtilis. J Bacteriol 81:741–746\nL83: \nL84:   * Armstrong RL, Hartford N, Kennett RH, St. Pierre ML, Sueoka N (1970) Experimental methods for Bacillus subtilis. In: Tabor H, Tabor CW (eds) Methods in enzymology, Vol 17A, Academic Press, New York pp 36–59\nL85: \nL86:   * Burke WF Jr, Le HT (1980) Characterization of a Bacillus subti