utton: Create RSS ] [Button: Cancel ]\nL128: \nL129: RSS Link [Input: Your RSS Feed Link] [Button: Copy ]\nL130: \nL131: ### Full text links\nL132: \nL133: 【8†Springer†dx.doi.org】\nL134: \nL135: 【3†Full text links】\nL136: ### Actions\nL137: \nL138: Cite\nL139: \nL140: Collections\nL141: \nL142: Add to Collections\nL143: \nL144: [Input]\nL145: \nL146:   * [Input]Create a new collection\nL147:   * [Input]Add to an existing collection\nL148: \nL149: Name your collection: [Input]\nL150: \nL151: Name must be less than 100 characters\nL152: \nL153: Choose a collection: [Select]\nL154: \nL155: Unable to load your collection due to an error\nL156: 【3†Please try again】\nL157: \nL158: [Button: Add ][Button: Cancel ]\nL159: \nL160: Display options\nL161: \nL162: Display options\nL163: \nL164: Format [Select]\nL165: ### Experimental Resource\nL166: \nL167: Linked Discoveries\nL168: \nL169: [Button: Appl Microbiol Biotechnol ]\nL170: \nL171: Actions\nL172: \nL173:   * 【9†Search in PubMed】\nL174:   * 【10†Search in NLM Catalog†www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov】\nL175:   * 【3†Add to Search】\nL176: \nL177: . 2008 May;79(2):263-72.\nL178: \nL179: doi: 10.1007/s00253-008-1425-2.\nL180: # Development of chemically defined medium for Mannheimia succiniciproducens based on its genome sequence\nL181: \nL182: 【11†Hyohak Song】^{  【12†1】 }, 【13†Tae Yong Kim】, 【14†Bo-Kyeong Choi】, 【15†Seong Jun Choi】, 【16†Lars K Nielsen】, 【17†Ho Nam Chang】, 【18†Sang Yup Lee】\nL183: \nL184: Affiliations Expand\nL185: ### Affiliation\nL186: \nL187:   * ^{1} Department of Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering (BK21 Program), KAIST, 335 Gwahangno, Yuseong-gu, Daejeon 305-701, Republic of Korea.\nL188: \nL189:   * PMID: 18379780\nL190:   * DOI: 【19†10.1007/s00253-008-1425-2†doi.org】\nL191: \nL192: Item in Clipboard\nL193: # Development of chemically defined medium for Mannheimia succiniciproducens based on its genome sequence\nL194: \nL195: Hyohak Song et al. Appl Microbiol Biotechnol. 2008 May.\nL196: \nL197: Show details\nL198: \nL199: Display options\nL200: \nL201: Display options\nL202: \nL203: Format [Select]\nL204: \nL205: [Button: Appl Microbiol Biotechnol ]\nL206: \nL207: Actions\nL208: \nL209:   * 【9†Search in PubMed】\nL210:   * 【10†Search in NLM Catalog†www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov】\nL211:   * 【3†Add to Search】\nL212: \nL213: . 2008 May;79(2):263-72.\nL214: \nL215: doi: 10.1007/s00253-008-1425-2.\nL216: ### Authors\nL217: \nL218: 【11†Hyohak Song】^{  【20†1】 }, 【13†Tae Yong Kim】, 【14†Bo-Kyeong Choi】, 【15†Seong Jun Choi】, 【16†Lars K Nielsen】, 【17†Ho Nam Chang】, 【18†Sang Yup Lee】\nL219: ### Affiliation\nL220: \nL221:   * ^{1} Department of Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering (BK21 Program), KAIST, 335 Gwahangno, Yuseong-gu, Daejeon 305-701, Republic of Korea.\nL222: \nL223:   * PMID: 18379780\nL224:   * DOI: 【19†10.1007/s00253-008-1425-2†doi.org】\nL225: \nL226: Item in Clipboard\nL227: \nL228: [Button: Full text links ]Cite\nL229: \nL230: Display options\nL231: \nL232: Display options\nL233: \nL234: Format [Select]\nL235: \nL236: Linked Discoveries\nL237: ## Abstract\nL238: This study presents a novel methodology for the development of a chemically defined medium (CDM) using genome-scale metabolic network and flux balance analysis. The genome-based in silico analysis identified two amino acids and four vitamins as non-substitutable essential compounds to be supplemented to a minimal medium for the sustainable growth of Mannheimia succiniciproducens, while no substitutable essential compounds were identified.\nL239: The in silico predictions were verified by cultivating the cells on a CDM containing the six non-substitutable essential compounds, and it was further demonstrated by observing no cell growth on the CDM lacking any one of the non-substitutable essentials. An optimal CDM for the enhancement of cell growth and succinic acid production, as a target product, was formulated with a single-addition technique.\nL240: The fermentation on the optimal CDM increased the succinic acid productivity by 36%, the final succinic acid concentration by 17%, and the succinic acid yield on glucose by 15% compared to the cultivation using a complex medium. The optimal CDM also lowered the sum of the amounts of by-products (acetic, formic, and lactic acids) by 30%. The strategy reported in this paper should be generally applicable to the development of CDMs for other organisms, whose genome sequences are available.\nL241: 【21†PubMed Disclaimer】\nL242: ## Publication types\nL243: \nL244:   * [Button: Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't ]\nL245: \nL246: Actions\nL247: \nL248:     * 【22†Search in PubMed】\nL249:     * 【23†Search in MeSH†www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov】\nL250:     * 【3†Add to Search】\nL251: ## MeSH terms\nL252: \nL253:   * [Button: Culture Media / chemical synthesis ]\nL254: \nL255: Actions\nL256: \nL257:     * 【24†Search in PubMed】\nL258:     * 【25†Search in MeSH†www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov】\nL259:     * 【3†Add to Search】\nL260: \nL261:   * [Button: Culture Media / chemistry* ]\nL262: \nL263: Actions\nL264: \nL265:     * 【26†Search in PubMed】\nL266:     * 【25†Search in MeSH†www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov】\nL267:     * 【3†Add to Search】\nL268: \nL269:   * [Button: Fermentation ]\nL270: \nL271: Actions\nL272: \nL273:     * 【27†Search in PubMed】\nL274:     * 【28†Search in MeSH†www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov】\nL275:     * 【3†Add to Search】\nL276: \nL277:   * [Button: Genetic Engineering / methods ]\nL278: Actions\nL279: \nL280:     * 【29†Search in PubMed】\nL281:     * 【30†Search in MeSH†www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov】\nL282:     * 【3†Add to Search】\nL283: \nL284:   * [Button: Genome, Bacterial ]\nL285: \nL286: Actions\nL287: \nL288:     * 【31†Search in PubMed】\nL289:     * 【32†Search in MeSH†www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov】\nL290:     * 【3†Add to Search】\nL291: \nL292:   * [Button: Mannheimia / genetics ]\nL293: \nL294: Actions\nL295: \nL296:     * 【33†Search in PubMed】\nL297:     * 【34†Search in MeSH†www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov】\nL298:     * 【3†Add to Search】\nL299: \nL300:   * [Button: Mannheimia / growth & development ]\nL301: \nL302: Actions\nL303:     * 【35†Search in PubMed】\nL304:     * 【34†Search in MeSH†www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov】\nL305:     * 【3†Add to Search】\nL306: \n"
